# ROADMAP — Active Modernization Sprint & Milestone Locks
File: openOODA/ROADMAP.oot

This document defines the active sprint plan, verification gates, and milestone locks.
All engineering execution aligns with the 10 strategic governance pillars and Boyd's E-M engine.
Completed features and historical proof locks reside in SHIPPED.oot.

## 0. Release State & Baseline Floor

- Release State: v2.11.0 from `openOODA/ooda.pkg` (Generational SemVer `v<Floor>.<Thrust>.<Patch>`).
- Generational Floor (F=2): Gen 2 Compiler and Capability Runtime Substrate Floor.
- Boyd E-M Thrust (T=10): 2-space formatting and 10-board governance seal (ASD-STE100).
- Verification Patch (P=0): Synchronized across package manifests and 14 canonical boards.

## 1. Active Sprint: Core Architecture & Submodule Modernization

- Task R1 (Formatting and Auto-Formatter):
  Codify 2-space indentation, match arrow alignment, and pipeline rules in FORMAT.oot.
  Implement native in-process `ooda fmt` CLI tool with AST pretty-printer and `--check` linter mode.
  Status: open.

- Task R2 (Tactical Submodule Directory Restructuring):
  Reorganize fragmented flat files into cohesive domain directories with mandatory `mod.oo` entry points.
  Target subsystems: `oodac/emit/`, `oodac/ast/`, `oodac/types/`, `mcp/engine/`, `std/net/`.
  Status: open.

- Task R3 (Compiler Memory & Token Struct Migration):
  Replace legacy tab-separated string tokens with packed `struct Token { kind: Int, line: Int, col: Int, text: String }`.
  Implement linear zero-copy `StringBuilder` in `std/text/` backed by `&AllocCap`.
  Status: open.

- Task R4 (Single-Source-of-Truth Board Automation):
  Implement `openOODA/scripts/sync_boards.oo` to automatically derive version pins from `ooda.pkg`.
  Status: done. Proof: `openOODA/scripts/sync_boards.oo` (135 lines, SSoT OK, 14 boards 2-line validated).

- Task R5 (Standard Library Capability Attenuation):
  Audit and attenuate broad capability grants across `ooda/std/` to exact minimal tokens.
  Status: open.

## 2. Sprint Acceptance & Verification Gates

1. Gate 1 (Zero Enforcer Violations): `openOODA/scripts/enforcer.oo` returns `__FAILS__=0`.
2. Gate 2 (Board Hygiene): `openOODA/scripts/check_board.oo` returns `OK` across 14 boards.
3. Gate 3 (Capability Gating): `ooda/qa/tests_onboarding/run_all_onboarding_tests.oo` passes 27/27 suites.
4. Gate 4 (8-Dimensional Adversarial Seal): `openOODA/scripts/redteam_hook.oo` emits `MASTER_RELEASE_SEAL: EMITTED`.
5. Gate 5 (Strict Line Limits): 100% of `.oo` and `.oot` files satisfy <= 256 lines.
6. Gate 6 (Negative-Trust Residual): Unverified items classified as Residual per falsification pipeline — see SHIPPED.oot GENERATED marker.
